  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile scvi RNA is strong (~0.65 accuracy), image-only models are weak, and the only multimodal test so far (config_038: scvi, ViT-L, transformer, concat) reaches 0.721 accuracy with supporting F1, suggesting that multimodal fusion is promising but only concat has been evaluated. This experiment tests whether weighted fusion improves over concat while keeping the RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed. It is the best next experiment because it directly extends the current best configuration, isolates the fusion design choice, and has high expected performance while reducing uncertainty about how to combine modalities under a limited budget."
